### 35 missed calls
Certain recent events I will not elaborate upon further in the interest of privacy for those involved have led me on an interesting train of
thought towards considering how I want to be perceived. I had always believed that as this train would not arrive at any stations related to
school or work, that it was not a train worth boarding for any reason. Moreover, I did not believe I had paid requisite fares to board this train
at all.

However, blocking out time to entertain this train of thought and conversing with people who have likely rode this train in the past make
me worried that it may be better for me to follow this train to its terminus station. However, as there are multiple possible lines and the conductor
is being a bitch and refuses to tell me which one we're on, I will need to use more of my surrounding context to determine which station I am to arrive at.

In CTA terms, it seems plausible that this train of thought could be headed to Skokie, or maybe Evanston. It is somewhat unlikely that I would be headed to
O'Hare or Cicero, although many seem to suggest this is the case.

None of this makes sense and it isn't meant to.

